I was addicted to old hack several years ago and only recently have
been becoming familiar with nethack. I always considered rings of
conflict distasteful and was prone to throw them away.  (Of course, I
haven't faced the huge room level or the new improved Wizard of
Yendor.)

There's been a lot of talk here as to how to moderate its power, the
most popular suggestion (the checkerboard effect) my least favorite --
just strikes me as ugly. My favorite of the suggestions I've seen was
just have it burn food like crazy.

I have another suggestion, though, that I haven't seen here (though I
may have just missed it). It's colored, of course, by my distaste for
the things, and I rather doubt people'll like it, but what the heck.

Make conflict affect the player. Just as with stun and confusion, the
game ignores any movement commands (or rest commands in this case, I
suppose) you make and instead moves your toward the nearest creature,
or if you're adjacent to creatures, you bash on one at random. You
still ultimately have this degree of control: you can remove the ring.
(A cursed ring of conflict would be _bad_, but that could be moved
toward the top of the list of things your god'll fix during prayer.)

This would add some interesting strategies to its use -- the player
would have to seriously consider whether to put it on in a roomful of
nasties... or maybe to go hide first. The player'd have to worry about
beating his or her own pets to death. And, of course, trying on rings
whose cursedness is unknown or that you know to be cursed would become
an even riskier proposition.

